PLR 6.2.7 clash dedup for COMPUTED keys over enumerated literals:
keys arrive as unfolded arithmetic trees (0 % 2, "a" + "b") --
simplify_expr folds them before canonical_key, so the dedup (first
key position, last value) fires for every computed-key family.
